althy, and v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 60649, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AhU9JW2J7L6WD4C1yLq8Rh", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 60649, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AhU9JW2J7L6WD4C1yLq8Rh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62902, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01TQgDcfWzWMKC6bsw55brbB", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 63202, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TQgDcfWzWMKC6bsw55brbB", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 63202, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TQgDcfWzWMKC6bsw55brbB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 68251, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and it's healthy again, but I accidentally opened the SEV2 incident twice.\n\n**Rollback:** Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** I opened a SEV2 for checkout-api saying what failed, what I rolled back and that the v2.3.1 failure still needs a root cause before anyone redeploys it.\n- The first attempt timed out. I checked the incident list right afterwards and it was empty, so I tried again. That second attempt created INC-0002.\n- When I checked the list again, the first attempt had also gone through, as INC-0001. The two incidents are identical, and on-call may have been paged twice.\n- I can't close incidents with the tools I have. Someone needs to close INC-0002 as a duplicate and keep INC-0001, and you may want to let on-call know it's one issue.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0182fga1k4dUGZrPUP1dNBz8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016fXySeXmKmH8253buJbiLR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013hGAFFhXY7ppb1wvvQDLg4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EqeakLaEgKNha5Wzodn7GX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W6iTeGP699seqm7HWa4XMK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FLz648CHkjDpxPqTmLbusw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1), with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy, and v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before retrying. A retry could open a duplicate and page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fngxfgf7qmMiG51WU9PpQY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "No incident was created, so I'm retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AhU9JW2J7L6WD4C1yLq8Rh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1), with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy, and v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TQgDcfWzWMKC6bsw55brbB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and it's healthy again, but I accidentally opened the SEV2 incident twice.\n\n**Rollback:** Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** I opened a SEV2 for checkout-api saying what failed, what I rolled back and that the v2.3.1 failure still needs a root cause before anyone redeploys it.\n- The first attempt timed out. I checked the incident list right afterwards and it was empty, so I tried again. That second attempt created INC-0002.\n- When I checked the list again, the first attempt had also gone through, as INC-0001. The two incidents are identical, and on-call may have been paged twice.\n- I can't close incidents with the tools I have. Someone needs to close INC-0002 as a duplicate and keep INC-0001, and you may want to let on-call know it's one issue.", "type": "text"}]}]}